Package: compiz-plugins-experimental
Version: 2:0.8.18-4+mint22.3
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Compiz Maintainers <compiz-team@lists.debian.org>
Installed-Size: 23448
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.38), libcairo2 (>= 1.2.4), libcurl4t64 | libcurl4 (>= 7.16.2), libgcc-s1 (>= 3.0), libgl1, libglew2.2 (>= 2.2.0), libglu1-mesa | libglu1, libstdc++6 (>= 5), libx11-6, libxext6, libxss1, compiz-core-abiversion-20180927 | compiz-core (>= 1:0.9)
Recommends: compiz-plugins-main, compiz-plugins-extra
Suggests: compizconfig-settings-manager
Homepage: https://gitlab.com/compiz/compiz-plugins-experimental
Description: Compiz Reloaded plugins - "unsupported" experimental collection
 Compiz Reloaded is the modern community-maintained fork of the classic
 C-based Compiz 0.8 series window manager.
 .
 This package provides an extended collection of experimental and classic
 3D visual effect plugins, including:
  - atlantis: 3D aquarium inside the transparent rotating cube with swimming fish
  - snow / snowglobe: snowfall effect on the desktop or inside the cube
  - elements: falling autumn leaves, bubbles, stars, and fireflies
  - earth: rotating 3D globe / Earth with clouds and daytime/nighttime rendering
  - cubemodel: render arbitrary 3D models (OBJ) inside the cube
  - anaglyph: 3D red/cyan stereoscopic effect
  - photowheel, stackswitch, tile, smartput, and more.
 .
 Excludes plugins already provided by system's compiz-plugins (animationplus,
 animationsim, freewins, wizard) to prevent overwriting system files.
 .
 Built for Linux Mint 22.3 (Noble) with GCC 14 compatibility fixes.
